### Setting up GitHub Pages
---
The first step to setting up your own GitHub Pages site is to create your GitHub account.
The guide I will be using will be from the official documentation here: [Quickstart for Github Pages]([Quickstart for GitHub Pages - GitHub Docs](https://docs.github.com/en/pages/quickstart))

1. The first step after creating your account is to create a new repository.

![Create Repository](/assets/images/gitub_pages_crete_repo.png)


2. The next step is to add a name to your repository. You can also add a description if you want. The name has to be in this format: `username.github.io`
	From there you can then just create it and you will be lead to a new page

![Repository Name](/assets/images/github_pages_repo_name.png)


3. Now this is where you create your `index.md` and use Markdown to create your homepage. Make sure to name it `index.md` and add whatever you want to your home page. Make sure to add this header:
```
---
layout: default
title: Home
---
```

![Create Index File](/assets/images/github_pages_create_index.png)


4. From here you can deploy your site!! Just go to your repository settings and go to the pages section.  Make sure that it is set to `Deploy from branch` and `main` at `/(root)`. This is where your site is going to deploy from.

![Deploy Settings](/assets/images/github_pages_deploy.png)

5. Now you can make a new page. For this example, create an `about.md` file and place your content in there or you can copy what I did. The same header as the index page, just with the title of the new page.
```
---
layout: page
title: About
---

## About Me

This is my about page.
```

6. Next is your config file. This is where you can choose a theme and add  your navigation bar. Create a new file named `_config.yml`. You can choose any theme you would like, some have less features than others so keep that in mind. [List of Themes](https://github.com/pages-themes)
```
theme: minima

header_pages:
  - index.md
  - about.md
```

7. After making all these changes, your site should look like this

![Final Site](/assets/images/github_pages_page.png)
